  "notes": "Slot = 4 bytes {u8 id, u8 count, u8 flag, u8 0}. Byte 2 (flag) controls how the count is drawn and MUST be set: 0x00 = no number (keys, herbs, F. Aid Spray), 0x01 = green number (weapons, F. Aid Box), 0x0D/0x0E = blue number (ammo), 0x05/0x09 = other colours used for flame/acid rounds, 0x16 = red percentage (Assault Rifle, count 100 = 100%). Verified: R. Launcher x5 flag 01 -> '5', H. Gun Bullets x60 flag 0D -> blue '60', same with flag 00 -> no number, Assault Rifle flag 16 count 100 -> '100%'. Jill has 10 slots (cursor grid 2x5). Names/counts appear after the status screen is reopened; icons of newly written ids are NOT redrawn until the game loads them (cell stays blank), same as RE2. Other inventory-shaped arrays exist at 0x0D21DC and 0x0D2274 (look like the other character's / stored inventories, e.g. for the Carlos segments) - not verified, write 0x0D2134 for the active character. WARNING: 0x0BDDD4 looks like an HP but is an enemy's HP, not Jill's.",
  "verified": "2026-10-07 live: start inventory (Easy) at 0x0D2134 = [0F 64 16][82 FA 00][83 01 00][84 01 00][2A 03 01] matched the status screen (Assault Rifle 100%, Reloading Tool, Game Inst. A/B, F. Aid Box 3: rei/re3s_3.jpg). Write test rei/re3_write_verify.jpg. HP: 0x0CCC90 tracked damage (200->140->140->80 with CONDITION Fine/Fine/Caution, rei/k1-3.jpg); wrote 15 -> 'Danger' (rei/re3_hp15.jpg), wrote 200 -> 'Fine' (rei/re3_hp200.jpg). Frames are in the agent scratchpad rei/."
